{"name":"Lake Winnipeg","hex":"#80a1b0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Lake Winnipeg","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A large lake in Manitoba, Canada."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Lake_Winnipeg"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lake Winnipeg","blocks":[{"text":"Lake Winnipeg is a 24,514-square-kilometre (9,465-square-mile) lake in North America, in the Canadian province of Manitoba. Its southern end is about 55 kilometres north of the namesake city, Winnipeg. It is the 12th largest lake on Earth, Canada's sixth-largest freshwater lake, and the third-largest freshwater lake contained entirely within Canada. It is relatively shallow, with a mean depth of 12 metres [39 feet]. Its deepest section is a narrow 36-metre (118-foot) deep channel between the northern and southern basins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Lake_Winnipeg_map.png/330px-Lake_Winnipeg_map.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Winnipeg","wikidata":"Q3272"},{"title":"Lake","blocks":[{"text":"A lake is often a naturally occurring, relatively large and fixed body of water on or near the Earth's surface. It is localized in a basin or interconnected basins surrounded by dry land. Lakes lie completely on land and are separate from the ocean, although they may be connected with the ocean by outflowing rivers. Lakes, like other bodies of water, are part of the water cycle, the processes by which water moves around the Earth. Most lakes are fresh water and account for almost all the world's surface freshwater, but some are salt lakes with salinities even higher than that of seawater. Lakes vary significantly in surface area and volume of water, but in total cover approximately 2.5 × 106 km2 (less than 2%) of the Earth's surface."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Lake_Idro_Italy_2005-08-16.jpg/330px-Lake_Idro_Italy_2005-08-16.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake","wikidata":"Q23397"},{"title":"Winnipeg","blocks":[{"text":"Winnipeg is the capital and largest city of the Canadian province of Manitoba. It is centred on the confluence of the Red and Assiniboine rivers. As of 2021, Winnipeg had a city population of 749,607 and a metropolitan population of 834,678, making it Canada's sixth-largest city and eighth-largest metropolitan area. In 2025, the city's estimated population reached 850,260."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Winnipeg%2C_Manitoba.jpg/330px-Winnipeg%2C_Manitoba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winnipeg","wikidata":"Q2135"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/NASA_Lake_Winnipeg.jpg/500px-NASA_Lake_Winnipeg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/NASA_Lake_Winnipeg.jpg/1280px-NASA_Lake_Winnipeg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/NASA_Lake_Winnipeg.jpg/500px-NASA_Lake_Winnipeg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"NASA false-colour image of Lake Winnipeg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANASA_Lake_Winnipeg.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Hecla_Island_and_Provincial_Park_in_Lake_Winnipeg_Manitoba_%2814%29.JPG/500px-Hecla_Island_and_Provincial_Park_in_Lake_Winnipeg_Manitoba_%2814%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Hecla_Island_and_Provincial_Park_in_Lake_Winnipeg_Manitoba_%2814%29.JPG/1280px-Hecla_Island_and_Provincial_Park_in_Lake_Winnipeg_Manitoba_%2814%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Hecla_Island_and_Provincial_Park_in_Lake_Winnipeg_Manitoba_%2814%29.JPG/500px-Hecla_Island_and_Provincial_Park_in_Lake_Winnipeg_Manitoba_%2814%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"American white pelicans loaf near shore, Hecla-Grindstone Provincial Park","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHecla_Island_and_Provincial_Park_in_Lake_Winnipeg_Manitoba_(14).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Gimli_Manitoba_Canada_Panorama.jpg/500px-Gimli_Manitoba_Canada_Panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Gimli_Manitoba_Canada_Panorama.jpg/1280px-Gimli_Manitoba_Canada_Panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Gimli_Manitoba_Canada_Panorama.jpg/500px-Gimli_Manitoba_Canada_Panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gimli on Lake Winnipeg.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGimli_Manitoba_Canada_Panorama.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Sunset_at_nordhouse_dunes.jpg/500px-Sunset_at_nordhouse_dunes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Sunset_at_nordhouse_dunes.jpg/500px-Sunset_at_nordhouse_dunes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sunset over Lake Michigan at Nordhouse Dunes in Manistee National Forest, Michigan, United States","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASunset_at_nordhouse_dunes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Casti