ion of New Zealand.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALake_Kaniere.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Nowitna_river.jpg/500px-Nowitna_river.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Nowitna_river.jpg/500px-Nowitna_river.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Nowitna River in Alaska. Two oxbow lakes – a short one at the bottom of the picture and a longer, more curved one at the middle-right.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANowitna_river.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}